<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Caucasus</p><h1 class="st-title">Terek Cossack Host</h1><p class="st-meta">1577 CE – 1920 CE (approx.) · capital Vladikavkaz</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The self-governing Cossack community of the Terek river, for over three centuries Russia's armed frontier society in the North Caucasus.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Free <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossacks</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/don-river">Don</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga">Volga</a> settled on the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/terek-river">Terek</a> in the 16th century, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greben-cossacks">Greben Cossacks</a> lived in the foothills. The host traditionally dates its founding to 1577, when Russian Cossacks were recorded on the Terek after Muscovy's push down the Volga to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/astrakhan">Astrakhan</a>. They served the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/tsardom-of-russia">Tsardom of Russia</a> in return for pay and freedoms.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossack</a> villages, or stanitsas, elected atamans and held assemblies, combining farming, fishing, vineyards and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horse-breeding">horse breeding</a> with military service. Many were <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-believers">Old Believers</a>. Under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> the host manned the fortified Caucasian Line from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kizlyar">Kizlyar</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mozdok">Mozdok</a>, was steadily placed under state control, and was formally reorganised in 1860 with its centre at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vladikavkaz">Vladikavkaz</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After 1917 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/terek-river">Terek</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossacks</a> briefly joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mountainous-republic-of-the-northern-caucasus">Mountainous Republic of the Northern Caucasus</a>, then fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/communist-party-of-the-soviet-union">Bolsheviks</a>. In 1920 the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/russian-sfsr">Russian SFSR</a> crushed them, abolished the host and deported many stanitsas, giving their lands to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chechens">Chechens</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ingush-people">Ingush</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/terek-cossack-host.jpg" alt="Terek Cossack Host" width="320" height="302"><figcaption>Image: Karl Piratsky · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:345_Changes_in_uniforms_and_armament_of_troops_of_the_Russian_Imperial_army.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1577 CE – 1920 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Vladikavkaz</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Mikhail Karaulov</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Russian Orthodox Christianity, Old Believers</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Russian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/russia">Russia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Terek Cossacks, Terek Cossack Army</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1748&amp;focus=terek-cossack-host" aria-label="Terek Cossack Host on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5758 650 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Terek Cossack Host lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6078 906L5820 533M6078 906L6487 457M6078 906L6078 906M6078 906L5820 533"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5820 533h0M6487 457h0M6078 906h0M5820 533h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6078 906h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6078 906h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Vladikavkaz. <a href="/atlas?year=1748&amp;focus=terek-cossack-host">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

